From 1f6c5e214d8cfd20a22e6e163ec0892a271fde19 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: crayon <hicrayon@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:57:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gateway: a reply to another agent carries no Codex account
 events (#4482)

The ChatGPT backend says what it thinks of its own account before the
reply, in codex.rate_limits (the account's windows) and
codex.response.metadata (the model list's tag). Only Codex has names for
those, and it reads its limits from them. A Responses client with a typed
event enum reads an event it has no name for and gives up on the whole
turn: Grok Build answered
"Couldn't read the response: serialization error: unknown variant
`codex.rate_limits`, expected one of `response.created`, ..." and the
user saw the turn die with no reply.

passthrough now runs the stream through codexLeadTidy for a Responses
relay to a client that is neither Codex's User-Agent nor a key owned by
the codex agent, dropping every frame whose event name or data type is
in the backend's own codex. namespace. Codex's own request keeps the
stream as it came. The quota tap (codexLimitsTap) and failover's sniff
read the upstream bytes before the filter, so limit accounting and
failover classification still see those events.

Verified with TestCodexLeadEventsStayWithCodex: it fails without the
filter (a nil leadTidy gives "event codex.rate_limits there=true, want
false" for a client with no User-Agent and for Grok Build's) and passes
with it, green under -race -count=20. gofmt -l clean; go vet ./...,
GOOS=linux go vet -tags nogui ./... and GOOS=windows go vet ./... clean,
and the matching three builds. internal/gateway as a whole keeps only
the four reds it had before this change on this macOS machine, already
filed as #3045, #3680 and #3547, and go test -tags nogui ./... has 79
packages ok with those and internal/plugin's #2207 (Bun 1.4.4) red.
